# Vulnerability findings deliberately suppressed from build.sh's scan report.
#
# The scan reports and does not fail the build, so a suppression only removes a
# finding from the report — which is exactly why it has to say why. The rule,
# enforced by build.sh before it scans (an entry breaking it fails the build): every entry is a finding ID on
# its own line, immediately preceded by a comment saying why it is safe to
# suppress — for example that the vulnerable code path is not reachable from
# sighop, or that no fixed version has shipped for the base image yet — and,
# ideally, when it should be looked at again. An entry without a reason fails
# the build. Suppressed findings are still printed (--show-suppressed).
#
# There are no entries.
